-- title:
--   Twisted elliptic–central fold as weighted twisted orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields which is Galois with $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ such that every $\tau$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$; let $0<\alpha<\beta$. Let $\Phi$ be a subset of the band $B=\{g : \|\det g\|_{\mathbb A_L}\in[\alpha,\beta]\}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ which is a fundamental domain for the image of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ under [`AutomorphicForm.globalPoints`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L15) with respect to adelic Haar measure restricted to $B$; let $\nu_Z$ be a Haar measure on $(\mathbb A_L)^\times$ and $\Omega$ a fundamental domain for the image of $L^\times$; let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum, i.e. a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to ring automorphisms of $\mathbb A_L$, continuous and compatible with $L\to\mathbb A_L$, through which $\sigma$ acts on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$; let $\xi:(\mathbb A_L)^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ be a character, continuous as a $\mathbb C$-valued function and trivial on $L^\times$; and let $\varphi$ be continuous with compact support on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$. Write $S$ for the set of $\delta\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose twisted norm class [`LT.TwistedNorm.normClassMap hgen (SigmaConjClasses.mk σ δ)`](def/TwistedNormClasses.html#L766) is the conjugacy class of some $\gamma\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ that is elliptic (its characteristic polynomial has no root in $K$) or central (a scalar matrix). Let $R\subseteq S$ be such that every $\delta\in S$ has a unique $\delta_0\in R$ with $\delta = u\cdot h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(h)$ for some $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and scalar $u\in L^\times$; for each $\delta_0\in R$ let $\Psi(\delta_0)\subseteq B$ be a fundamental domain, for the restricted Haar measure, for the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_L)$ of the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{t : t\delta_0\sigma(t)^{-1}=\delta_0\}$ of $\delta_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$; and let $\Theta$ be a fundamental domain for $\nu_Z$ for the image in $(\mathbb A_L)^\times$ of $\{\sigma(w)/w : w\in L^\times\}$. Then $$\int_\Phi\int_\Omega \xi(z)\sum_{\delta\in S}\varphi\big(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(zx)\big)\,d\nu_Z\,dg=\sum_{\delta_0\in R} n(\delta_0)^{-1}\int_\Theta \xi(z)\int_{\Psi(\delta_0)}\varphi\big(x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(zx)\big)\,dg\,d\nu_Z,$$ where $\sigma$ acts on adelic matrices through $D$, scalars $z$ enter as the central scalar matrix, the sums over $S$ and $R$ are finite sums in the `finsum` sense, and $n(\delta_0)$ is the number of classes in $L^\times/\{\sigma(w)/w\}$ represented by some $u\in L^\times$ with $u\,\delta_0=h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(h)$ for some $h\in\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$.
--
--   This is the geometric unfolding step for the $\sigma$-twisted kernel on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over a cyclic extension: the elliptic-and-central part of the twisted sum, folded against the character $\xi$ over a fundamental domain for the centre, is rewritten as a sum of twisted orbital integrals over twisted centraliser domains, weighted by the reciprocals of the finite numbers $n(\delta_0)$ of scalar ambiguities. It is used by the later statements producing the factorised form of the twisted elliptic–central fold and its comparison with the untwisted kernel fold.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_setIntegral_twistedCentralEllipticFold_eq_finsum_inv_card_mul_setIntegral_sigmaCentralizerDomain.lean

